6 Discussion
This paper describes an approach to collision avoidance for mobile robots equipped with synchro-drives. Based on the exact motion equations of such robots, it derives an approximate version that models robot trajectories by nite sequences of circular arcs. The dynamic window approach rst prunes the overall search space by considering only the next steering command. This results in a two-dimensional search space of circular trajectories. After that, the search space is reduced to the admissible velocities allowing the robot
